# IntroMesh

- Read `docs/DESIGN.md` before any UI. Reuse tokens and shadcn components; do not mix another visual library.
- Separate UI (`src/app`, `src/components` with `onboarding/`, `signal/`, `share/`), use cases (`src/server`), domain (`src/domain`), persistence (`src/lib/store`, `src/lib/supabase`), Meta (`src/lib/meta`), and session (`src/lib/session`).
- Strict TypeScript. Validate external inputs and outputs with Zod.
- `MODEL_API_KEY` and `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` only on the server. No `NEXT_PUBLIC_` for secrets.
- Discovery requires consent. Do not invent rows, matches, or model text. Synthetic data carries the `demo` mark.
- Do not compare every profile to every other. Deterministic candidates first; the model only explains recommendations already chosen.
- Product-facing copy is English for the Meta hackathon.
- Before closing a task, run `npm test` and `npm run lint` when the change affects them. Without a key, do not claim Meta responds.
- Product detail: `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`, `docs/PRIVACY.md`, `docs/PRODUCT.md`, `AGENTS.md`.
